#. type: Title =
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/high-elves.adoc:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "High Elves"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/high-elves.adoc:18
msgid ""
"image:high-elves/logo.webp[width=91,height=90,float=\"right\"] The Elven "
"Kingdoms are the most ancient and cultured of all the world’s realms aside "
"from those of the cold-blooded Lizardmen races. Long before the crude "
"townships of men took shape the Elves were building glittering cities in the "
"island-continent of Ulthuan. Soon more cities arose in their colonies "
"throughout the world. After millennia of habitation many of these cities "
"still exist. They are graced by fantastical towers, sweeping arches, and a "
"thousand other wonders undreamed of by mankind. Within soaring spires the "
"High Elves pursue their age-long studies of art, sorcery and the world both "
"natural and otherwise."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/high-elves.adoc:28
msgid ""
"The Elven mind is not only keen but is matched by a near perfect physique "
"and extraordinary longevity. Elves resemble men but are taller and more "
"elegantly proportioned with long athletic limbs. They have lean, intelligent "
"and handsome faces with delicately pointed ears and entrancing almond shaped "
"eyes. It has been said that their swift precise movements make the most "
"graceful human seem oafish in comparison. These qualities make them "
"dangerous warriors as well as unparalleled craftsmen and sorcerers."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/high-elves.adoc:35
msgid ""
"Elves are not warlike by nature as are, for example, Orcs and even Dwarfs "
"and men to some extent. However they are proud -some say arrogant – and "
"ultimately confident in their purpose.  Thousands of years ago the Elves and "
"Dwarfs fought a long and bitter war over possession of the Old World – a war "
"fuelled by pride and suspicion on both sides."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/high-elves.adoc:44
msgid ""
"This war weakened the two races to such an extent that both were nearly "
"destroyed as a result. Much of the Dwarf realm was subsequently overrun by "
"greenskins, the Elves were driven from their cities in the Old World, and "
"the Elven homelands were plunged into the devastating civil war known as The "
"Sundering. Elves and Dwarfs have never forgotten that war and it remains a "
"source of recrimination and antagonism between them to this day."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/high-elves.adoc:62
msgid ""
"Although their strength is less than it once was the Elven Kingdoms "
"constitute the greatest bastion against Chaos in the world. Millennia ago – "
"when the Age of Chaos began – the most adept of the High Elf Mages "
"constructed a gigantic vortex of power at the centre of the island-continent "
"of Ulthuan at the heart of the Elven Kingdoms. The purpose of this vortex "
"was to draw magical energy out of the world, which was at that time overrun "
"with daemons and other wholly sorcerous creatures.  By means of a system of "
"magical standing stones arranged around the circular island like a spider’s "
"web, the power of Chaos was gradually drawn away and stability restored. The "
"Daemon armies were destroyed or banished back to the Realms of Chaos from "
"which they had come. This is a burden that the High Elves carry to this day. "
"Were Ulthuan and its vortex to fall the world would be quickly consumed in "
"magic and mortal creatures would cease to exist – at least in any form "
"recognisable as such."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/high-elves.adoc:74
msgid ""
"The Elven Kingdoms remain eternally alert to the threat of Chaos. They are "
"the undisputed masters of the seas and have fortresses situated all over the "
"globe at strategic positions.  There they wait and watch the lights of magic "
"playing upon the northern skies, and prepare for the next battle against the "
"forces of Chaos. However, their numbers are fewer now than ever, and the "
"burden of defence grows ever more heavy. For this reason the Elves regard "
"the human realms as vital to the eternal battle against Chaos, for if the "
"human realms fell it would be only a question of time before Ulthuan itself "
"would be overwhelmed by the tides of Chaos."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/high-elves.adoc:77
#, no-wrap
msgid "High Elf army selector"
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/high-elves.adoc:82
#, no-wrap
msgid "include::partial$high-elves.tsv[]\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/high-elves.adoc:86
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[archers,†1]]1. Archers"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/high-elves.adoc:91
msgid ""
"High Elf archers add +1 to their dice roll when making Shooting attacks. "
"They will therefore score a hit against targets in the open on a 3 or more, "
"against targets that are defended on a 4 or more, and against fortified "
"targets on a 5 or more."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/high-elves.adoc:92
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[giant-eagles,†2]]2. Giant Eagles"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/high-elves.adoc:94
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[dragons,†3]]3. Dragons"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/high-elves.adoc:97
msgid ""
"Dragons can fly. Dragon rider units and any other units that include a "
"Dragon riding character cause terror in their enemies."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/high-elves.adoc:108
msgid ""
"Because Dragon Riders have a great many hits (6) which are difficult to "
"inflict even during a lengthy combat engagement, we must consider the "
"possibility of hurting the Dragon and reducing its effectiveness in "
"subsequent turns. Therefore, if a Dragon Rider has accumulated 4–5 hits by "
"the end of the Shooting phase or Combat phase and is no longer engaged in "
"combat it is deemed to have been badly hurt. Once a Dragon has been badly "
"hurt all accumulated hits are discounted and its maximum hits value and "
"Attacks are halved for the rest of the battle (to 3 Hits and 3/2 Attacks)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/high-elves.adoc:114
msgid ""
"Generals, Wizards and Heroes can ride Dragons. A Dragon can fly increasing "
"its rider’s move to 100cm. An extra [.edit]#+3/3# Attacks are added to those "
"of its rider. A Dragon can breathe fire if the character has joined a unit "
"that isn’t engaged in combat."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/high-elves.adoc:121
msgid ""
"Dragons can make a fiery breath. This applies both to a unit of Dragon "
"Riders and to Dragons ridden by characters that have joined a unit of "
"troops. The fire breath has a range of 20cm. Breath can be directed against "
"one target as for normal shooting and has 3 Attacks that are worked out in "
"the usual way at 4+ to hit."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/high-elves.adoc:122
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[elven-bolt-thrower,†4]]4. Elven Bolt Thrower"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/high-elves.adoc:125
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[wizard,†5]]5. Wizard"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/high-elves.adoc:129
msgid ""
"High Elf Mages are especially powerful wizards and to represent this can re-"
"roll a failed spell on any dice result except a 1. If a spell is failed "
"because a 1 is rolled then no re-roll is permitted."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/high-elves.adoc:130
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[giant-eagle-mount,†6]]6. Giant Eagle Mount"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/high-elves.adoc:133
msgid ""
"Generals, Wizards and Heroes can ride a Giant Eagle. An Eagle can fly "
"increasing its rider’s move from 60 to 100cm. An extra +2 Attacks are added "
"to those of its rider."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/high-elves.adoc:136
msgid ""
"Generals, Wizards and Heroes can ride Chariots. An extra +1 Attack is added "
"to those of its rider."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/high-elves.adoc:139
#, no-wrap
msgid "High Elf spells"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/high-elves.adoc:141
#, no-wrap
msgid "Storm of Stone"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/high-elves.adoc:147
msgid ""
"_The ground erupts around the Mage, and a hail of stones, rocks and dirt "
"hurls itself upon his foes._"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/high-elves.adoc:149
msgid "This spell affects every enemy unit within range."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/high-elves.adoc:156
msgid ""
"Every enemy unit within range takes 3 Attacks worked out in the normal way. "
"Unengaged units are not driven back by the Storm of Stone (the assault comes "
"from the ground beneath their feet). Engaged units carry over any hits "
"scored into the first round of combat; any hits scored count as having been "
"struck in the combat itself."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/high-elves.adoc:157
#, no-wrap
msgid "Light of Battle"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/high-elves.adoc:163
msgid ""
"_A radiant light shines forth upon the Mage’s companions filling them with "
"magical vigour._"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/high-elves.adoc:171
msgid ""
"The spell lasts for the duration of the following Combat phase.  Every unit "
"and every character that has joined a unit gains a bonus +1 attack. These "
"attacks can be allocated to any stand in the unit and can be allocated to a "
"different stand in each combat round."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/high-elves.adoc:172
#, no-wrap
msgid "Heaven’s Fire"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/high-elves.adoc:178
msgid ""
"_The mage imbues the Elven archers with an unearthly swiftness enabling them "
"to rain death upon the enemy._"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/high-elves.adoc:183
msgid ""
"This spell can be cast upon a friendly unit of unengaged missile armed "
"infantry or cavalry within range. It cannot be cast on artillery. The Mage "
"does not need to be able to see the friendly unit nor their intended target."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/high-elves.adoc:189
msgid ""
"When the Heaven’s Fire spell is cast on a unit, it can shoot twice that turn "
"instead of once. If it has already shot that turn it can therefore shoot "
"again immediately. If it has yet to shoot it can shoot twice. When a unit "
"shoots twice due to Heaven’s Fire the second shot is always at a −1 penalty "
"to hit."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/high-elves.adoc:190
#, no-wrap
msgid "Hail of Destruction"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/high-elves.adoc:196
msgid ""
"_A hail of fiery arrows flies from the Mage’s outstretched finger tips and "
"strikes an enemy unit._"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/high-elves.adoc:200
msgid ""
"This spell can be cast on an enemy unit. The Mage must be able to see his "
"target to use this spell. The spell cannot be directed at a unit engaged in "
"combat."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/high-elves.adoc:205
msgid ""
"The Hail of Destruction is treated like three ordinary shooting attacks (4+ "
"to hit) except that armour has no effect (all targets count as having no "
"armour). A unit can be driven back by a Hail of Destruction as with ordinary "
"shooting."
msgstr ""
